{
  "format": "zapterm-command-lists",
  "version": 1,
  "platform": "cisco_ios",
  "notes": "Cisco IOS / IOS-XE command lists. Every command below was checked against Cisco's documentation — nothing was added from memory: • Command Reference, Cisco IOS XE 17.15.x (Catalyst 9300): Interface and Hardware, IP Addressing Services, Layer 2/3, Network Management, Security, Stack Manager and High Availability, System Management, Unicast Routing and VLAN chapters • Cisco IOS IP Routing: BGP Command Reference (show ip bgp … through Z) • IP Routing Configuration Guide, Cisco IOS XE 17.x: BGP 4 • Cisco IOS Security Command Reference (A to C; S to Z: show crypto …) • Cisco IOS First Hop Redundancy Protocols Command Reference • Embedded Packet Capture: Command Reference, Configuration Guide IOS XE 17, Catalyst 9000 Management Configuration Guide • Security and VPN Configuration Guide IOS XE 17.x: Crypto Conditional Debug Support • \"Understand Important Information on Debug Commands\" (undebug all, terminal monitor) • IP Addressing Services Configuration Guide 17.15 (DHCP snooping) Left out: commands that reload or erase the device, and ones not found in those documents (e.g. \"show processes cpu sorted\", \"show vrf\"). Safety review: the EPC capture stops by itself (monitor capture … limit duration <s> packets 1000, per the EPC command reference, whose default is no limit) and the debugs carry a caution quoting Cisco’s “Important Information on Debug Commands” (“Enabling debugging can disrupt router operation, especially when the network is under heavy load”).",
  "label": "Cisco IOS / IOS-XE",
  "stopDebug": ["undebug all", "debug crypto condition reset"],
